 "result_text": "`HttpTransport` in `sentry_sdk/transport.py` no longer uses `Hub`. I haven't run the test suite or any other check, so the change is untested.\n\nI made two edits:\n- **`__init__`:** removed the `from sentry_sdk import Hub` import and the `self.hub_cls = Hub` assignment. Nothing else in the SDK read `hub_cls`.\n- **`capture_envelope`:** removed the `hub = self.hub_cls.current` lookup and the `with hub:` block in `send_envelope_wrapper`. The wrapper now just runs `_send_envelope` and `_flush_client_reports` inside `capture_internal_exceptions()`.\n\nThe old code ran the send on the worker thread under the hub captured when the envelope was queued. I didn't add a scope-based replacement, so the send now runs under whatever scope the worker thread has by default. If a test depends on the send running under the caller's scope, it will show up there.",
